1
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:09,410
With another man?

2
00:00:09,410 --> 00:00:11,000
Seriously?

3
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:14,480
Is it anyone I know?

4
00:00:14,480 --> 00:00:16,450
No.

5
00:00:16,450 --> 00:00:21,310
He worked for a club
specializing in women's needs.

6
00:00:21,310 --> 00:00:25,370
I happened to bump into him the other day.

7
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:28,650
A club?

8
00:00:28,650 --> 00:00:33,560
I didn't realize the experience
meant so much to you.

9
00:00:35,710 --> 00:00:38,000
I also questioned myself.

10
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:44,260
Was sex really so important to me?

11
00:00:46,660 --> 00:00:48,230
But...

12
00:00:53,670 --> 00:01:00,000
I now know I'm a 31 year old woman
who can have proper wants.

13
00:01:04,970 --> 00:01:06,430
Sorry.

14
00:01:07,900 --> 00:01:10,540
That's not a revelation
to be proud of, is it?

15
00:01:13,130 --> 00:01:16,220
I know you treated me well.

16
00:01:19,750 --> 00:01:23,840
I'm so sorry I've hurt you.

17
00:01:27,130 --> 00:01:30,250
[Divorce Forms]

18
00:01:31,750 --> 00:01:36,380
I see. So you told Ouji everything.

19
00:01:36,380 --> 00:01:37,800
Yeah.

20
00:01:40,450 --> 00:01:45,010
Actually, same here.

21
00:01:45,010 --> 00:01:46,380
Huh?

22
00:01:46,380 --> 00:01:48,250
I'll be getting a divorce.

23
00:01:48,250 --> 00:01:49,740
What?

24
00:01:49,740 --> 00:01:51,460
I told my husband everything.

25
00:01:51,460 --> 00:01:54,020
L-Like, "everything"?

26
00:01:54,020 --> 00:01:58,640
Yup. We're discussing the arrangements
as we speak.

27
00:01:59,330 --> 00:02:03,190
What will happen to Chizuka?

28
00:02:03,190 --> 00:02:06,830
We'll be fighting over her custody.

29
00:02:06,830 --> 00:02:10,460
But I'll be paying him
a settlement fee regardless.

30
00:02:10,460 --> 00:02:13,110
I see.

31
00:02:13,110 --> 00:02:21,060
Everyone's making serious confessions, huh?

32
00:02:22,400 --> 00:02:25,400
You started it, Akina.

33
00:02:25,400 --> 00:02:27,350
Yeah.

34
00:02:27,350 --> 00:02:29,080
Huh?

35
00:02:29,080 --> 00:02:33,310
Watching your honorable confession

36
00:02:34,320 --> 00:02:37,300
lit a fire in my heart.

37
00:02:37,300 --> 00:02:40,040
Honorable...

38
00:02:40,970 --> 00:02:42,730
That's one way to put it.

39
00:02:42,730 --> 00:02:47,650
My confession was far from honorable.

40
00:02:48,580 --> 00:02:55,490
I saw how Ouji treasured our relationship,

41
00:02:55,490 --> 00:02:59,240
and knew I couldn't keep secrets anymore.

42
00:03:57,710 --> 00:04:01,770
[Finale]

43
00:04:01,770 --> 00:04:04,570
[Saint Love Survivors]

44
00:04:06,420 --> 00:04:09,520
[What lies after a "happy end"?]

45
00:04:12,990 --> 00:04:17,000
A divorce.

46
00:04:20,640 --> 00:04:22,050
Excuse us.

47
00:04:22,050 --> 00:04:24,260
Kazahaya is ready for you.

48
00:04:24,260 --> 00:04:28,240
Good morning.
I'll be your makeup artist for today.

49
00:04:28,240 --> 00:04:30,180
Good morning.

50
00:04:34,740 --> 00:04:36,820
Fuyumi.

51
00:04:41,280 --> 00:04:43,470
Is it true you got divorced?

52
00:04:46,840 --> 00:04:49,210
We're still fighting over it.

53
00:04:57,430 --> 00:04:59,400
I'm so sorry.

54
00:05:01,540 --> 00:05:03,150
I...

55
00:05:05,330 --> 00:05:07,940
I logically knew it was wrong.

56
00:05:09,680 --> 00:05:12,110
But couldn't talk myself out of it.

57
00:05:15,590 --> 00:05:18,660
And now, I've messed up your family.

58
00:05:19,880 --> 00:05:22,820
Shota, I already had issues with my husband.

59
00:05:22,820 --> 00:05:28,070
Meeting you just gave me the resolve
to file a divorce.

60
00:05:31,030 --> 00:05:35,610
I'm sorry to make you feel responsible.

61
00:05:40,470 --> 00:05:42,120
But, I...

62
00:05:47,010 --> 00:05:50,640
No crying before an important shoot.

63
00:05:51,750 --> 00:05:55,040
Raise your head.

64
00:05:59,440 --> 00:06:03,420
You're an actor, right?

65
00:06:07,850 --> 00:06:09,840
Use that to your advantage.

66
00:06:39,590 --> 00:06:44,350
I had sex with another man.

67
00:06:47,910 --> 00:06:49,380
Why?

68
00:07:12,490 --> 00:07:14,040
Haru!

69
00:07:25,640 --> 00:07:28,600
That's NTR, right?

70
00:07:28,600 --> 00:07:29,520
Huh?

71
00:07:29,520 --> 00:07:31,040
"Netorare".

72
00:07:31,040 --> 00:07:33,800
When you get excited seeing your girl

73
00:07:33,800 --> 00:07:36,050
get it on with another guy.

74
00:07:36,050 --> 00:07:37,980
The hell? Is that a kink?

75
00:07:37,980 --> 00:07:42,330
Can be. It helps reignite some couples, too.

76
00:07:42,330 --> 00:07:44,100
Maybe your friend's in a similar boat?

77
00:07:44,100 --> 00:07:48,000
Well... Who knows.

78
00:07:48,880 --> 00:07:51,220
But in the case of NTR,

79
00:07:51,220 --> 00:07:56,230
the guy isn't looking at their partner
until she's taken, right?

80
00:07:56,230 --> 00:07:57,540
He's disrespecting his girl.

81
00:07:57,540 --> 00:07:59,220
There you are.

82
00:07:59,220 --> 00:08:00,720
Keiko. You here for a shoot?

83
00:08:00,720 --> 00:08:02,740
Yeah. The livestream just ended.

84
00:08:02,740 --> 00:08:05,860
I was looking everywhere for you.

85
00:08:05,860 --> 00:08:09,610
Maybe I was disrespecting her.

86
00:08:10,170 --> 00:08:11,120
Huh?

87
00:08:11,120 --> 00:08:13,800
I thought being with her would be easy.

88
00:08:13,800 --> 00:08:15,620
She was cute.

89
00:08:15,620 --> 00:08:18,900
She wouldn't make romance a pain.

90
00:08:19,460 --> 00:08:23,410
I thought she would always love me.

91
00:08:23,410 --> 00:08:28,030
The cool guy she's come to know.

92
00:08:31,810 --> 00:08:33,830
I'm so lame.

93
00:08:33,830 --> 00:08:37,080
And for our lame narcissist, I have a gift.

94
00:08:37,080 --> 00:08:38,900
Hey, that's that popular novel.

95
00:08:38,900 --> 00:08:40,020
Does Ouji even read?

96
00:08:40,020 --> 00:08:42,820
I'm not interested in books, or fads.

97
00:08:42,820 --> 00:08:44,540
Just read it.

98
00:08:44,540 --> 00:08:47,830
I can't believe I'm pulling an assist.

99
00:08:47,830 --> 00:08:49,200
But we'll call it even here.

100
00:08:49,200 --> 00:08:52,230
What does that... Hey!

101
00:08:56,150 --> 00:08:58,600
[Saint Love Survivors]

102
00:09:13,960 --> 00:09:15,990
This is...

103
00:09:18,100 --> 00:09:20,220
<i>I made a prayer to God.</i>

104
00:09:20,220 --> 00:09:24,780
<i>I didn't care what role I played in his life.</i>

105
00:09:24,780 --> 00:09:30,490
<i>I simply wanted to be a part of it.</i>

106
00:09:32,160 --> 00:09:35,670
<i>But that is most likely where our marriage...</i>

107
00:09:36,900 --> 00:09:39,810
"Went wrong".

108
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:53,240
[Ouji]

109
00:09:59,460 --> 00:10:02,540
[Haru, I read your book]
[I want to see you]

110
00:10:06,610 --> 00:10:09,700
<i>The book... Like, my book?</i>

111
00:10:09,700 --> 00:10:13,140
<i>H-How did he find out?</i>

112
00:10:13,140 --> 00:10:15,040
[I want to see you]

113
00:10:17,410 --> 00:10:20,530
He's going to ask for a divorce.

114
00:10:20,530 --> 00:10:22,650
[This weekend, Izu. How about it?]

115
00:10:23,210 --> 00:10:26,150
Huh? Izu?

116
00:10:29,280 --> 00:10:32,840
[Izu-Kogen Station]

117
00:10:44,880 --> 00:10:47,400
I came here with the guys once.

118
00:10:47,400 --> 00:10:48,940
Huh?

119
00:10:48,940 --> 00:10:51,620
It's a bit cliche, but it's a nice place.

120
00:10:54,170 --> 00:11:00,000
But... Why Izu?

121
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:02,110
I wanted to visit a hot spring, remember?

122
00:11:02,110 --> 00:11:04,650
I do, but...

123
00:11:05,390 --> 00:11:08,580
Wait, we're staying overnight?

124
00:11:08,580 --> 00:11:10,030
Yeah.

125
00:11:10,030 --> 00:11:12,330
Oh, don't worry. The inn has most amenities.

126
00:11:12,330 --> 00:11:14,730
That's not why I'm confused.

127
00:11:16,630 --> 00:11:21,450
Aren't we... getting a divorce?

128
00:11:21,450 --> 00:11:23,600
- I wonder.
- Huh?

129
00:11:23,600 --> 00:11:25,650
Come on, let's go.

130
00:11:28,020 --> 00:11:30,600
There, I got a big one.

131
00:11:30,600 --> 00:11:33,200
Nice.

132
00:11:33,200 --> 00:11:35,480
Which one next...

133
00:11:35,480 --> 00:11:37,400
Your crepe, sir.

134
00:12:01,550 --> 00:12:04,240
[Inatori Akao Hotel]

135
00:12:11,980 --> 00:12:16,430
I'm glad you're looking better.

136
00:12:32,240 --> 00:12:36,140
Should we visit the inner garden?

137
00:12:36,140 --> 00:12:37,420
Huh?

138
00:12:43,750 --> 00:12:46,560
It sure gets chilly at night.

139
00:12:46,560 --> 00:12:48,440
Want an extra layer?

140
00:12:48,440 --> 00:12:49,710
Why?

141
00:12:49,710 --> 00:12:51,060
Huh?

142
00:12:51,630 --> 00:12:54,150
I know you're mad.

143
00:12:54,150 --> 00:12:57,280
I know you're in disbelief.

144
00:12:57,280 --> 00:13:00,020
- Huh?
- Don't avoid the subject.

145
00:13:00,800 --> 00:13:03,940
You read the book, didn't you?

146
00:13:06,490 --> 00:13:07,890
I did.

147
00:13:07,890 --> 00:13:10,760
- Then why...
- At first, I was stunned.

148
00:13:10,760 --> 00:13:13,500
You didn't even tell me you were an author.

149
00:13:13,500 --> 00:13:15,260
Sure, you didn't give exact names,

150
00:13:15,260 --> 00:13:18,410
but did you really need to detail everything?

151
00:13:20,880 --> 00:13:22,490
Sorry.

152
00:13:24,030 --> 00:13:29,040
One particular passage
shook me more than anything.

153
00:13:32,320 --> 00:13:38,560
"That is most likely
where our marriage went wrong".

154
00:13:42,580 --> 00:13:48,430
You said every decision you made, was wrong.

155
00:13:50,780 --> 00:13:52,140
No, well...

156
00:13:52,820 --> 00:13:57,820
That's a "me" problem.

157
00:14:03,390 --> 00:14:07,530
Entertaining book, though.

158
00:14:08,170 --> 00:14:09,300
Huh?

159
00:14:09,300 --> 00:14:12,740
Your book.

160
00:14:15,180 --> 00:14:18,770
Maybe that's not much,

161
00:14:18,770 --> 00:14:23,200
coming from a guy who doesn't read.

162
00:14:23,200 --> 00:14:27,210
But at some point,
I stopped caring about the whodunits,

163
00:14:27,210 --> 00:14:28,990
and let myself get absorbed in the story.

164
00:14:29,690 --> 00:14:32,390
It's like I joined the protagonist
on her adventure.

165
00:14:33,910 --> 00:14:36,380
I learned you're an amazing individual, Haru.

166
00:14:38,240 --> 00:14:43,090
Guess what I learned on my second read?

167
00:14:43,090 --> 00:14:47,460
This guy is objectively the worst.

168
00:14:47,460 --> 00:14:48,490
He's an idiot.

169
00:14:48,490 --> 00:14:49,820
No, that's not...

170
00:14:49,820 --> 00:14:52,050
I'm an idiot, too.

171
00:14:52,820 --> 00:14:55,320
I'm an idiot,

172
00:14:55,320 --> 00:14:57,410
but even I can tell.

173
00:15:01,400 --> 00:15:04,840
This book's a love letter.

174
00:15:08,920 --> 00:15:11,940
I can't believe you had so much to say.

175
00:15:17,060 --> 00:15:20,860
You still love me, don't you?

176
00:15:25,950 --> 00:15:27,790
What the heck?

177
00:15:32,150 --> 00:15:34,840
You assume I "still love you"?

178
00:15:36,060 --> 00:15:37,710
Isn't that obvious?

179
00:15:39,300 --> 00:15:41,810
Of course I still love you.

180
00:15:44,710 --> 00:15:46,360
I love your face.

181
00:15:46,360 --> 00:15:49,180
I love your voice, mannerisms, tobacco scent,

182
00:15:49,180 --> 00:15:52,700
bony hands, and the way you wear your boots.

183
00:15:57,300 --> 00:15:59,010
But...

184
00:16:01,240 --> 00:16:02,870
What I truly,

185
00:16:05,250 --> 00:16:07,810
really love about you...

186
00:16:12,340 --> 00:16:16,810
Is that you don't doubt my love for you.

187
00:16:19,270 --> 00:16:24,250
Your honestly dense kindness

188
00:16:26,630 --> 00:16:29,810
has accepted me, time and time again.

189
00:16:32,810 --> 00:16:35,000
Despite how pathetic a person

190
00:16:36,920 --> 00:16:39,840
I actually am.

191
00:16:51,320 --> 00:16:53,040
No, I...

192
00:16:54,390 --> 00:16:56,680
I haven't treated you well at all.

193
00:16:59,650 --> 00:17:01,840
You're an idiot.

194
00:17:01,840 --> 00:17:04,720
You're happy I don't question your love?

195
00:17:05,830 --> 00:17:08,560
I really am a narcissist.

196
00:17:08,560 --> 00:17:10,790
Well, that's...

197
00:17:11,830 --> 00:17:17,230
How can you love me, when I'm so lame?

198
00:17:21,890 --> 00:17:23,620
I'm sorry.

199
00:17:26,040 --> 00:17:29,590
I'm sorry I made you think you were pathetic.

200
00:17:32,480 --> 00:17:34,590
I'm sorry I made you cry.

201
00:17:44,900 --> 00:17:49,400
Maybe our marriage did go wrong.

202
00:17:51,620 --> 00:17:53,180
But...

203
00:17:55,350 --> 00:17:57,450
We can still right our wrongs, right?

204
00:18:23,840 --> 00:18:27,660
This trip is our official honeymoon.

205
00:18:45,110 --> 00:18:48,640
What the... is this another one of my dreams?

206
00:18:48,640 --> 00:18:51,600
Huh? No. This is real.

207
00:18:51,600 --> 00:18:53,490
What?

208
00:18:53,490 --> 00:18:55,500
You okay?

209
00:18:55,500 --> 00:18:58,820
What about you? Are you okay?

210
00:18:58,820 --> 00:19:03,750
I actually really want to do it.

211
00:19:03,750 --> 00:19:05,520
With you, specifically.

212
00:19:05,520 --> 00:19:06,830
Huh?

213
00:19:06,830 --> 00:19:14,590
Actually, the other night I, uh...
had a reaction for once.

214
00:19:14,590 --> 00:19:16,470
Wanna know why?

215
00:19:18,670 --> 00:19:21,610
You had a dream, about me?

216
00:19:22,420 --> 00:19:27,340
Apparently it happens.
It's called NTR, or something.

217
00:19:27,340 --> 00:19:29,250
Perv.

218
00:19:30,900 --> 00:19:36,890
But I've felt dreamy
seeing you do it out back

219
00:19:36,890 --> 00:19:40,780
with a complete stranger, too.

220
00:19:40,780 --> 00:19:43,050
What? When did that happen?

221
00:19:43,050 --> 00:19:45,850
I guess we're a pair of perverts, huh?

222
00:19:45,850 --> 00:19:47,820
You can say that again.

223
00:20:55,350 --> 00:20:57,470
I can get it in part way.

224
00:20:57,470 --> 00:21:00,230
Damn it, this is so frustrating.

225
00:21:00,230 --> 00:21:02,000
Don't be so hard on yourself.

226
00:21:02,970 --> 00:21:05,580
I felt really good.

227
00:21:05,580 --> 00:21:10,070
But I have to show up Mr. Delivery Guy.

228
00:21:10,070 --> 00:21:11,770
Aw...

229
00:21:11,770 --> 00:21:13,300
Here, I have an idea.

230
00:21:16,950 --> 00:21:19,300
Let me put in some effort.

231
00:21:22,220 --> 00:21:25,230
No, I...

232
00:21:26,140 --> 00:21:28,090
I'll put in my effort, too.

233
00:21:31,330 --> 00:21:33,370
Wait, morning already?

234
00:21:36,040 --> 00:21:38,400
Wow...

235
00:21:38,400 --> 00:21:41,070
The sun's already coming up.

236
00:21:43,170 --> 00:21:45,370
It's 5AM in the morning.

237
00:21:45,370 --> 00:21:47,530
Which means I lasted 6 hours.

238
00:21:47,530 --> 00:21:52,020
At least I outdid him on time.

239
00:21:52,020 --> 00:21:54,340
That's amazing.

240
00:21:55,250 --> 00:22:01,560
If we don't go all the way,
we can mess around forever.

241
00:22:12,830 --> 00:22:14,560
Haru.

242
00:22:15,410 --> 00:22:17,300
I love you.

243
00:22:19,000 --> 00:22:20,850
Marry me?

244
00:22:21,800 --> 00:22:26,460
Too bad. We already are, dummy.

245
00:22:32,070 --> 00:22:32,970
[One year later]

246
00:22:32,970 --> 00:22:35,200
Fuyumi.

247
00:22:35,200 --> 00:22:38,980
Congratulations on the divorce!

248
00:22:38,980 --> 00:22:41,920
I can't believe it ended, just like that.

249
00:22:41,920 --> 00:22:45,350
It helped that he found
another partner for himself.

250
00:22:45,350 --> 00:22:49,970
An assistant 15 years his junior, right?
What a shocker.

251
00:22:50,470 --> 00:22:52,340
How's your love life going, Akina?

252
00:22:52,340 --> 00:22:56,910
Actually...

253
00:22:56,910 --> 00:23:00,080
I've begun seeing someone, sort of.

254
00:23:00,080 --> 00:23:02,260
That's news to me.

255
00:23:02,260 --> 00:23:04,650
- Who is it?
- He's a normal guy.

256
00:23:04,650 --> 00:23:07,730
A coworker who confessed to me.

257
00:23:07,730 --> 00:23:11,040
Nothing bad with normal, I guess.

258
00:23:15,270 --> 00:23:16,870
He looks... kind.

259
00:23:16,870 --> 00:23:19,440
You're allowed to say he looks bland.

260
00:23:19,440 --> 00:23:23,570
We did finally have sex, though.

261
00:23:24,920 --> 00:23:26,410
Also normal, by the way.

262
00:23:26,410 --> 00:23:29,370
Your standards are just way too high.

263
00:23:29,370 --> 00:23:30,910
You can't compare him to a professional.

264
00:23:30,910 --> 00:23:35,950
Aw, but I gave him the time to be pent up.

265
00:23:37,630 --> 00:23:41,330
We're sort of all like survivors.

266
00:23:41,330 --> 00:23:42,670
Survivors?

267
00:23:42,670 --> 00:23:44,610
Survivors of love.

268
00:23:46,380 --> 00:23:49,750
We each had our trials and tribulations,

269
00:23:49,750 --> 00:23:51,640
<i>but we all fought through it, together.</i>

270
00:23:51,640 --> 00:23:53,050
<i>A survivor...</i>

271
00:23:53,050 --> 00:23:56,070
<i>That is what we are, yeah.</i>

272
00:23:57,550 --> 00:24:00,440
How is your love life going, Haru?

273
00:24:19,390 --> 00:24:21,000
Morning.

274
00:24:41,530 --> 00:24:45,030
[Saint Love Survivors]

